{{/*
  404.html.tmpl — dist/404.html.

  Built by renderNotFound (build.go), NOT by the pages loop in Run: it must
  never contribute a Path to the sitemap. Dot is a notFoundPage, which embeds
  page directly (no wrapper type beyond that) — same pattern as
  about.html.tmpl and legal.html.tmpl, plus its own NoIndex field that always
  overrides page's site-derived one to true (see notFoundPage's doc comment
  in build.go).

  Content is a short signpost, not an essay: the site's editorial voice,
  pointing back at the two places a lost visitor actually wants — the
  portfolio and a way to get in touch.
*/}}
{{define "404"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{{template "head" .}}
</head>
<body>
{{template "header" .}}
<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">404</span>
      <h1>This page has left the cellar.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The page you're looking for isn't here &mdash; it may have moved, or the address
        wasn't quite right. From here, the full portfolio is the surest way onward, and the team is
        always glad to help you find what you're after.</p>
      {{/* The address that failed. Seeing it is often the whole answer: a
           truncated paste or a stray character is obvious on sight.
           Revealed by notfound.js, so it stays hidden with JS off rather
           than showing an empty frame. */}}
      <p class="notfound-asked" hidden>You asked for <code id="notfound-path"></code></p>
      <p class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/portfolio/">Browse the Portfolio</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact/">Contact Us</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{/* Where assets/js/notfound.js writes what it found. It reads the path
       the visitor asked for and searches the same catalog-index the
       portfolio filters against, so a delisted wine or a moved slug still
       leads somewhere useful instead of dead-ending on a signpost.

       Empty and hidden server-side: with JS off, or if the index fetch
       fails, the page is exactly the signpost it was before. */}}
  <section class="wrap">
    <div id="notfound-suggest" class="notfound-suggest" data-index-url="{{.IndexURL}}" hidden></div>
  </section>
</main>
{{template "footer" .}}
<script src="{{.NotFoundJSURL}}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
{{end}}
